  "notes": "Modified cash basis audit. Governmental lines from the Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p5, Total Governmental Funds column); business-type lines from the Proprietary Funds statement (p7, Total Proprietary Funds column), which includes depreciation and rolls net position (measure net position). Business-type totals: no single printed total, operating + nonoperating added. Balance sheet: the page titled 'Statement of Activities - Modified Cash Basis' (p1) is the statement of net position; kept government-wide because it includes business-type capital assets, debt and interfund balances. No beginning cash printed (no prior-year column), so beginning_cash null; ending cash = governmental funds Cash and cash equivalents 203,017 (county treasurer 2,726 separate). 'Other operating revenues' categorized charges for services because the Statement of Activities charges for services column includes them. Detail: the only supplementary schedule is a combined all-funds Budgetary Comparison Schedule - Primary Government (pp8-9), so detail is per fund column of the governmental funds (p5) and proprietary funds (p7) statements; the budget schedule is not recorded. Business-type fund detail totals with nonoperating lines are computed (operating + nonoperating). Read pages 1-9 of 9"
}
